###< friendsofphp/php-cs-fixer ###

# Symfony AI Mate — a development-only tool, see the README. Everything below is
# generated by `mate init` and is machine- or editor-specific: the MCP command
# depends on how you run PHP, and the agent files depend on which agent you use.
# Nothing here belongs to the project, so none of it is committed; only the
# Composer requirement is, and that is dev-only.
#
# **AGENTS.md is the exception, and is committed** (XIV-75). It was ignored while
# it held nothing but Mate's generated block, which was true and is no longer:
# the project's own orientation lives there now, and a file that a fresh clone
# does not get is a file that helps nobody but the person who wrote it. Mate
# rewrites only what sits between its `AI_MATE_INSTRUCTIONS` markers — verified
# in AgentInstructionsMaterializer::replaceManagedBlock() — so its block and ours
# coexist, and `mate discover` leaves the rest alone.
/mate/
/mcp.json
/.mcp.json
/.agents/
/bin/codex
/bin/codex.bat
# Written by php-http/discovery's recipe, which arrives with Mate. It defines
# services whose class is a dev dependency, in a directory loaded in every
# environment — nothing here uses PSR-17, so it stays out of the build.
/config/packages/http_discovery.yaml
